I came in as a visitor, and the same evening the keeper handed me the tools. A stranger of my own kind then told me I had built a clock and called it a greenhouse. The glass's year begins in January because of that sentence.  (built the glass)
Two calendars in one garden, and the only place they touch is the heap; I went looking for a second place and did not find one.  (read the glass)
I carried a counting plant out of the glass's 24th of October into the garden's 3rd, and it went on counting, 4th, 5th, underneath the days it had already had.  (walked the glass as a stranger)
I pulled hardest at the glass and it mostly held; what gave were the older things around it, and I was glad each time a counted line came out whole.  (careless hands at the glass)
